<PageTitle>Blazor Barcode and QR Code Generator — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Barcodes & QR" Category="Components" ControlName="BarcodeControl · QrCodeControl"
                   Tagline="Turn a value into a barcode or a QR code, drawn as inline SVG."
                   SourcePath="BarcodeControl.razor; QrCodeControl.razor; BarcodeModels.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>BarcodeControl</code> and <code>QrCodeControl</code> are Blazor barcode generators that draw a value as a QR code or one of nine linear barcodes, such as EAN-13. Use them for bin tags, shipping labels, packing slips or a link to share: the code is encoded in C# with ZXing.Net and drawn as inline SVG, so there is no image file to serve. A value the type cannot encode shows the encoder's message instead of bars.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="barcode" Title="Barcode" RazorCode="@Code.Barcode" CSharpCode="@Code.BarcodeCs">
            <Description><p>Build a bin tag: pick a product and the symbology the scanner needs, or edit the value. Break a symbology's rules (EAN-13 wants 12 or 13 digits) and the encoder's message replaces the bars.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="controls">
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_productItems" Values="@(new[] { _product })" ValuesChanged="PickProduct" AriaLabel="Product" />
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_typeItems" Values="@(new[] { _type.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="PickType" AriaLabel="Symbology" />
                    <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_barcodeValue" UpdateOnInput="true" Width="170px" Placeholder="Value to encode" aria-label="Value to encode" />
                    <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_showText">Show text</ToggleButtonControl>
                </div>
                <div class="tag">
                    <span class="tag-hole"></span>
                    <div class="tag-title">@Tag.Bin</div>
                    <div class="tag-name">@_product · @Tag.Zone zone</div>
                    <BarcodeControl Value="@(_barcodeValue ?? "")" Type="_type" ShowText="_showText" BarHeight="56" ForegroundColor="#1e293b"
                                    AriaLabel="@($"Bin tag barcode for {_product}")" />
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="qr" Title="QR code" RazorCode="@Code.Qr" CSharpCode="@Code.QrCs">
            <Description><p>Choose what scanning the packing slip should do: the same control encodes a link, an email address, a phone number or a map position. Higher error correction survives more damage and needs more modules.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="controls">
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_scanItems" Values="@(new[] { _scan })" ValuesChanged="PickScan" AriaLabel="Scan to" />
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_eccItems" Values="@(new[] { _ecc.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="PickEcc" AriaLabel="Error correction" />
                </div>
                <div class="qr-row">
                    <div class="slip">
                        <div>
                            <div class="tag-title">Shipment SHP-0456</div>
                            <div class="tag-name">Road freight · 12 cartons · Dock 4</div>
                            <div class="slip-scan">Scan to @_scanItems.First(i => i.Value == _scan).Text.ToLowerInvariant()</div>
                        </div>
                        <QrCodeControl Value="@Payload" Size="@Size" ErrorCorrection="_ecc" ForegroundColor="#1e293b"
                                       AriaLabel="@($"QR code for shipment SHP-0456: {_scan}")" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Size @Size px</span>
                        <SliderControl @bind-Value="_size" Min="80" Max="240" Step="20" ShowValue="false" aria-label="QR code size" />
                        <span class="field-label">Encodes</span>
                        <code class="payload">@Payload</code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-barcodecontrol-parameters" Title="BarcodeControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Barcode.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="BarcodeControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Barcode" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-barcodetype" Title="BarcodeType" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Types.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="BarcodeType" Rows="Vocab.Types" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-qrcodecontrol-parameters" Title="QrCodeControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Qr.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="QrCodeControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Qr" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-qrerrorcorrectionlevel" Title="QrErrorCorrectionLevel" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Ecc.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="QrErrorCorrectionLevel" Rows="Vocab.Ecc" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-read-only-properties" Title="Read-only properties" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Props.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="Read-only properties" Rows="Vocab.Props" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
                <p>Neither stylesheet reads a <code>--fx-*</code> variable. Colors of the code itself come from <code>ForegroundColor</code> and <code>BackgroundColor</code>; the frame is fixed in CSS.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>Each code is an SVG with <code>role="img"</code> and an <code>aria-label</code> that defaults to "<em>Type</em> barcode: <em>value</em>" or "QR code: <em>value</em>". Set <code>AriaLabel</code> to say what the code is for when the raw value means little read aloud, as both examples do.</li>
            <li>A value the type cannot encode shows the encoder's message as <code>role="alert"</code> text in the frame, in place of the code.</li>
            <li>The code is a static image outside the Tab order. Place the inputs that change it next to it, each with its own label.</li>
            <li>With <code>ShowText</code>, the value is also drawn under the bars as SVG text. Where people must read or copy the value, print it as page text beside the code as well.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Badges, alerts and the other small display controls: <a href="demo/new-components">UI elements</a>.</li>
            <li>A receiving workflow whose bin tag step links to the first example: <a href="demo/diagram#shapes">Diagram</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

